#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:4
msgid "Submitting to the Asset Store"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:7
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:9
msgid "This tutorial aims to serve as a guide on how you can submit your own assets to the `Godot Asset Store <https://store.godotengine.org/>`_ and share them with the Godot community."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:13
msgid "As mentioned in the :ref:`doc_using_asset_store_website` page, in order to be able to submit assets to the Asset Store, you need to have a registered account, and be logged in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:18
msgid "Submission guidelines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:20
msgid "Before submitting your asset, please ensure it follows all of the requirements, and also consider following the recommendations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:24
msgid "Requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:26
msgid "Generally speaking, most assets people submit to the Asset Store are accepted. However, in order for your asset to be accepted, there are a few requirements it needs to meet to be approved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:30
msgid "The asset must **work**. If the asset doesn't run or otherwise doesn't work in the specified Godot version, then it will be rejected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:33
msgid "The asset must have a proper **.gitignore** file. It's important to keep redundant data out of the repository. `Here's a template. <https://raw.githubusercontent.com/aaronfranke/gitignore/godot/Godot.gitignore>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:37
msgid "No **submodules**, or any submodules must be non-essential. GitHub does not include submodules in the downloaded ZIP file, so if the asset needs the contents of the submodule, your asset won't work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:41
msgid "The **license** needs to be correct. The license listed on the Asset Store must match the license in the repository. The repository **must** have a license file, called either \"LICENSE\" or \"LICENSE.md\". This file must contain the license text itself and a copyright statement that includes the year(s) and copyright holder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:47
msgid "Use proper **English** for the name and description of your asset. This includes using correct capitalization, and using full sentences in the description. You can also include other languages, but there should at least be an English version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:52
msgid "The icon link must be a **direct link**. For icons hosted on GitHub, the link must start with \"raw.githubusercontent.com\", not \"github.com\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:56
msgid "Recommendations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:58
msgid "These things are not required for your asset to be approved, but if you follow these recommendations, you can help make the asset store a better place for all users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:62
msgid "When creating non-project assets, it is common practice to place your files inside of an **addons/asset_name/** folder. Do this to avoid having your files clash with other assets, or with the files of users installing your asset. This folder will **not** be automatically generated when a user installs your asset."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:67
msgid "Fix or suppress all script **warnings**. The warning system is there to help identify issues with your code, but people using your asset don't need to see them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:71
msgid "Make your code conform to the official **style guides**. Having a consistent style helps other people read your code, and it also helps if other people wish to contribute to your asset. See the :ref:`doc_gdscript_styleguide` or the :ref:`doc_c_sharp_styleguide`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:76
msgid "If you have screenshots in your repository, place them in their own subfolder and add an empty **.gdignore** file in the same folder (note: **gd**, not **git**). This prevents Godot from importing your screenshots. On Windows, open a command prompt in the project folder and run ``type nul > .gdignore`` to create a file whose name starts with a period."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:82
msgid "If your asset is a library for working with other files, consider including **example files** in the asset."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:85
msgid "Consider adding a **.gitattributes** file to your repository. This file allows giving extra instructions to Git, such as specifying line endings and listing files not required for your asset to function with the ``export-ignore`` directive. This directive removes such files from the resulting ZIP file, preventing them from being downloaded by Asset Store users. These are common examples of **.gitattributes**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:94
msgid "Projects / Templates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:101
msgid "Addons / Asset Packs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:113
msgid "If you are submitting a plugin, add a **copy** of your license and readme to the plugin folder itself. This is the folder that users are guaranteed to keep with their project, so a copy ensures they always have those files handy (and helps them fulfill your licensing terms)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:118
msgid "While the Asset Store allows more than just GitHub, consider hosting your asset's source code on **GitHub**. Other services may not work reliably, and a lack of familiarity can be a barrier to contributors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:123
msgid "Submitting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:125
msgid "Once you are logged in, click on **Upload Asset** on the top right of the website. It will take you to the following page:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:130
msgid "Here is a breakdown of each field:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:132
msgid "**Publisher**: This is the public name associated with the asset. For example, the XR Tools asset has the publisher \"Godot XR\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:135
msgid "**Publisher Name**: The name of the new publisher you are creating."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:137
msgid "**Publisher URL Slug**: how the publisher will appear in its link. For example, the XR Tools asset has the following URL: ``https://store.godotengine.org/asset/godot-xr/godot-xr-tools/``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:140
msgid "The publisher URL Slug in that is \"godot-xr\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:142
msgid "**Asset Name**: The name of your asset. Should be a unique, descriptive title of what your asset is."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:145
msgid "**Asset URL**: How the asset will be named in its link. For example, the XR Tools asset has the following URL: ``https://store.godotengine.org/asset/godot-xr/godot-xr-tools/``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:148
msgid "The asset URL for that link is \"godot-xr-tools\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:150
msgid "After filling out those fields, agree to the terms of service after reading them, and click \"Continue\". You will be brought to the asset's management page, where you can edit almost everything about how it will appear on the store, as well as upload different versions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:158
msgid "Management pages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:161
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:163
msgid "The overview tab lets you submit your asset for review. You can also view analytics including how many times it's been downloaded, page visits, and the number of people who have added it to their library."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:167
msgid "You can also delete the asset at the bottom of the page from this tab."
msgstr ""

