#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:183
msgid "Media"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:185
msgid "The media tab is where you upload your thumbnail, screenshots, an image for the featured page if you want, and link to a YouTube video if you have one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:189
msgid "Versions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:191
msgid "This is where you upload the actual asset files. For each version you upload you can give it a name, write a changelog, and specify the minimum Godot version (and maximum if applicable). There is also an additional information field for anything miscellaneous."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:196
msgid "Each individual version has a maximum file size of 1GB."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:199
msgid "Pricing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:201
msgid "While paid assets can't be uploaded yet, there are some settings relevant to free assets. You can link to another website where you accept donations, such as Patreon or Ko-Fi. You can also disable reviews if you want (in the future paid assets will **not** have this option)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:207
msgid "Submitting for review"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/community/asset_store/submitting_to_asset_store.rst:209
msgid "Once you are done, press \"Submit\". Your asset will be entered into the review queue. You will be informed when your asset is reviewed. If it was rejected, you will be told why that may have been, and you will be able to submit it again with the appropriate changes."
msgstr ""
